{#
  Stats band — the numbers, each one carried by a photograph.

  THE ONLY STATS BLOCK ON THE SITE. There used to be two: this one on /about/
  and a numbered, picture-less variant inside the private water supplies
  flagship, which quoted a different number of years. One component, one set of
  figures: change site.stats and every page that shows the band follows.

  THE YEARS FIGURE HAS TO MATCH THE PROSE. The band once read "30+" while five
  passages of copy said "twenty years" — /index.njk (the positioning body and
  the credentials list), the private water supplies positioning lead and the
  design-install FAQ. A reader gets both on the same screen, so they have to
  agree. Stefan's own "a water chemist of thirty years" on the home page is a
  DIFFERENT claim (his career, not the firm's age) and is deliberately left
  alone. If the firm's age changes, change it in site.stats and in those five
  passages together.

  The LABEL matters as much as the figure. It read "Years in the water
  industry", which is not the same claim as the firm's age, and on /about/ the
  band sits a screen below "graduated in 1993, and has worked in the water
  industry ever since" — 20+ against thirty-odd, on one page, under a heading
  saying "Invicta by the numbers". "Years in business" is the claim the figure
  actually supports, and it cannot collide with Stefan's own career.

  Content comes from `site.stats` by default, so a page normally includes this
  with no variables at all:

      {% include "stats-band.njk" %}

  Overrides, all optional:
    statsItems    an array in place of site.stats, same shape
                  ({ label, figure, image, alt })
    statsSurface  the section behind the band: omit for paper, or pass
                  "section--light" / "" (navy)
    statsId       suffix for the hidden heading's id, if two ever share a page
    statsHeading  the hidden heading itself

  A stat with no `image` simply has no picture; the figure and label still line
  up with the others, because the media sits at the foot of an equal-height
  column rather than setting the column's height. Such a stat is marked
  `stat--plain`, because on a phone the card is the photograph with the figure
  laid over it, and one without a picture needs the plain treatment back.
#}
{% set statsItems = statsItems or site.stats %}
{% if statsItems and statsItems.length %}
<section class="section {{ statsSurface if statsSurface is defined else "section--paper" }} stats-band"
         aria-labelledby="stats-band-title-{{ statsId or 'x' }}">
  <h2 id="stats-band-title-{{ statsId or 'x' }}" class="visually-hidden">{{ statsHeading or "Invicta by the numbers" }}</h2>
  <div class="container stats-band__grid">
    {% for s in statsItems %}
    <article class="stat{% if not s.image %} stat--plain{% endif %}">
      <div class="stat__text">
        <h3 class="stat__label">{{ s.label }}</h3>
        <p class="stat__figure">{{ s.figure }}</p>
      </div>
      {% if s.image %}
      <div class="stat__media">
        {# The frame that clips has to hug the picture, and .stat__media carries
           padding-top above it, so the parallax sits on an inner wrapper. #}
        <div class="parallax">
          <img src="{{ s.image }}" alt="{{ s.alt }}" width="1000" height="625" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
